  "behavioral_change": "SQLAlchemy v_old 1.4.46 to v_new 2.0.23. sqlalchemy.engine.Connection.execute no longer accepts raw SQL strings (text coercion removed, StatementImpl._text_coercion), and result rows change from dict-like LegacyRow to named tuples (Row.__getitem__).",
  "downstream_effect": "The downstream storage layer fails against a PostgreSQL sidecar and the scoring tests are frozen with the human test_patch.",
  "reference_fix": "In `kinto/core/cache/postgresql/__init__.py`, `kinto/core/permission/postgresql/__init__.py`, `kinto/core/storage/postgresql/__init__.py` and `kinto/core/storage/postgresql/migrator.py`, imports `sqlalchemy as sa` from `kinto.core.utils`, wraps every raw SQL string passed to `conn.execute(...)` in `sa.text(...)`, and switches result row access from dictionary indexing such as `row[\"last_modified\"]` to attribute access such as `row.last_modified`.",
